y mobile teeth.", "runs": [{"text": "Phenomenon"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "where"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "deciduous/primary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "teeth"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "replaced"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "permanent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "teeth."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "This"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "process"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occurring"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "between"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ages"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "5–12 years as a normal physiological change. Deciduous teeth should be left to fall out themselves unless the teeth are carious or there is any other indication. Parents should be counseled accordingly and be instructed to assist their children to loosen the already mobile teeth."}]}, {"id": "body-16955", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-16956", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Mixed dentition", "runs": [{"text": "Mixed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dentition"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "1146"}}, {"id": "body-16957", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Loose deciduous teeth", "runs": [{"text": "Loose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "deciduous"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "teeth"}], "list": {"level": 3, "numberingId": "1146"}}, {"id": "body-16959", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Investigation", "runs": [{"text": "Investigation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-16960", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "CBCT or OPG X-ray or/ and PA X-ray", "runs": [{"text": "CBCT"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "OPG"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "X-ray"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or/"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "PA"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "X-"}, {"text": "ray